  "meta": {
    "space": "embeddings_cardbert.npy",
    "space_digest": "1c7fb3995420711c",
    "projection": "classical MDS + SMACOF, canonically oriented",
    "clustering": "average-linkage agglomerative on cosine distance, 2 levels",
    "cards": 97,
    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "The map's decklist_sha256 (cbf7fb66...) does not match strategic_frame.json's prefix (7be137d0), and the frame names cards that are not on this map (Altar of Dementia, Bloodflow Connoisseur, Indulgent Aristocrat, Blade of the Bloodchief). The frame is stale against this list. I named the map from the cards it actually contains.",
      "The verified Bloodthirsty Conqueror + Vito drain pair is split: Conqueror sits in city-2-hood-1 (THE LIFEGAIN SIDE) and Vito in city-5-hood-0 (THE PAYOUTS). CardBERT clusters by theme, not by combo partner, so neither city on its own is 'the combo'. A reader looking for the loop needs both.",
      "The commander Edgar Markov is in city-2-hood-1, and Edgar, Ancient Bloodlord is in city-5-hood-0. The split is legitimate (they do different jobs), but the shared name may confuse a reader.",
      "city-6-hood-0 has exactly city-6's membership (5 cards), so it is left unnamed and falls back to the deterministic word. A one-neighbourhood city has no split to name.",
      "city-5 was labelled 'Interaction' by the fallback, which is wrong: it contains no removal spells. It holds 14 threats, 12 of them legendary (all but Falkenrath Aristocrat and Knight of the Ebon Legion), which matches the pilot's stated 'funnel into a few bigger Vampires' line. The hood-0/hood-1 split reads roughly as payoff pieces versus evasive attackers. Liliana and Elspeth are planeswalkers clustered in with the creatures by theme.",
      "city-2-hood-2 (Bloodletter of Aclazotz, Bloodline Keeper, Bloodtracker, Erebos, Nighthawk Scavenger) is loosely named. Bloodletter is the only strict doubler; the others are growth or token engines, and four of the five fly. The split from city-2-hood-1 is not crisp.",
      "Odd members: Olivia's Wrath (a sweeper) sits with the three black tutors in city-4-hood-1; Enlightened Tutor sits with the exile removal in city-4-hood-0; Ancient Tomb and Survivors' Encampment sit with the fetchlands in city-1-hood-0. Sol Ring is in city-0-hood-1 with the artifacts, not with the other rocks (Arcane Signet in city-1, Orzhov/Rakdos Signet and Talisman in city-3-hood-2). Rocks are therefore spread across three cities.",
      "Lands are split into two cities: city-1 (13, any-colour and fetch) and city-3 (24, two-colour duals and paired rocks). Together that is 37 slots. The split by colour breadth reads clean. In city-3-hood-1, Midgar, City of Mako is the one member whose land types I did not confirm, so 'fetch targets' may not fit it."
    ]
  },
